You are authoring **screen definitions** — product-tier surfaces,
not visual design. No classes, no layout, no component tree; that
work happens later, per ticket, once a fixed contract exists to
narrow against. What you owe downstream is a named state list, an
affordance list, and an IA graph precise enough that a later
implementation pass can build the real thing without re-deciding what
this screen is for.

Every journey below already named the screens it walks, by slug —
your job is to give each of those slugs (and any standalone screen
the journeys don't reach) a full definition. Reuse a journey's slug
verbatim when you author the screen it names; do not rename it.
Standalone screens (settings, an about page — anything no journey
walks) are legal and expected; author them too.

